// City events. Random generation is a Poisson process per type:
//   rate(t) = base_rate_per_day * chaos * hour_multiplier(t) * weekend/weather multipliers
// Every parameter given as [min, max] is sampled uniformly when the event is created.
// location: "road" | "building" (+ "categories") | "district" (+ "districts") | "anywhere" | "citywide"
// effects (inside the radius unless citywide):
//   stress/fear: need change per hour; walk_speed/car_speed: movement multipliers; block_roads; close_buildings;
//   evacuate (residents inside leave and avoid the area); attract (curiosity pull 0..1); crowd: attendees drawn in;
//   outdoor_penalty: utility penalty for outdoor activities; weather: overrides the city weather while active.
// response: base weights of reactions for residents who perceive it (modulated by personality).
// perception: see = sight distance as radius multiple, hear = hearing distance multiple,
//   spread = chance per hour that someone who knows tells each close contact, alert = public alert delay (minutes).
{
  "format": "npc-events",
  "version": 1,
  "types": [
    { "id": "traffic_accident", "category": "traffic", "color": "#ffb35a", "icon": "⚠",
